{"name":"Silver Mink","hex":"#9f8d7c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lustrous, white, metallic element, atomic number 47, atomic weight 107.87, symbol Ag.","Coins made from silver or any similar white metal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from silver.","Made from another white metal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver"},{"term":"mink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any semi-aquatic, carnivorous mammal in the Mustelinae subfamily, similar to weasels, with dark fur, native to Europe and America, of which two species in different genera are extant: the American mink (Neogale vison) and the European mink (Mustela lutreola).","The fur or pelt of a mink, used to make apparel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mink","blocks":[{"text":"Mink are dark-coloured, semiaquatic, carnivorous mammals in the genera Mustela and Neogale and part of the family Mustelidae, which also includes weasels, stoats, martens, otters, badgers, and others. There are two extant species referred to as \"mink\", the American mink and the European mink. The extinct sea mink was related to the American mink but was much larger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/American_Mink.jpg/330px-American_Mink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mink"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_crystal.jpg/330px-Silver_crystal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver"},{"title":"Silver (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver or metallic gray is a color tone resembling gray that is a representation of the color of polished silver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png/330px-Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Europ%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg/500px-Europ%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Europ%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg/500px-Europ%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"European mink (Mustela lutreola)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEurop%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg/500px-Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg/1280px-Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg/500px-Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg?ut